    REBEL 3.x has been developed to satisfy the demand for a spreadsheet
    that offers unlimited customization potential.  The entire spreadsheet 
    is patterned after a high level programming language.  By adding new 
    functions and utilities, it can be tailored to fit the needs of 
    virtually any user group. 
    
    REBEL requires no special license or registration fee to use, copy, or
    distribute. It may even be packaged with other products or services.
    For complete details, refer to the License Agreement in the back of the
    User's Manual. 



    ___________________________________________________
    REQUIREMENTS

         REBEL requires an IBM PC or compatible with at least 384K
         of memory, running DOS 2.1 or higher.


    ___________________________________________________
    DOCUMENTATION

         The User's Manual is contained in two files. To print
         it, use the dos PRINT or COPY command.  If possible,
         set your printer to 60 lines per page.

                  A:\>  print  CHAP1-4.DOC
                  A:\>  print  CHAP5-11.DOC
               or
                  A:\>  copy   CHAP1-4.DOC   PRN:
                  A:\>  copy   CHAP5-11.DOC  PRN:


    ___________________________________________________
    HOW TO RUN REBEL

         To start REBEL in Color Mode, type:

                  A:\>  REBEL


         To start REBEL in Black and White Mode, type:

                  A:\>  REBEL  -B


    ________________________________________________________
    SAMPLE WORKSHEETS

         Three sample worksheets have been included:

            CHECKS.RB2      (a checkbook management worksheet)
            COGO.RB2        (an example survey that uses many of
                             the Coordinate Geometry functions)
            MATRIX.RB2      (a general worksheet that contains an
                             example of each of the Matrix Algebra
                             functions)

         To load a worksheet, press the F3 function key twice from
         the Root Function Key Menu, and enter the worksheet's name
         (with or without the extension).



    ________________________________________________________
    STANDARD SCRIPT LIBRARY

         Scripts are one of the most powerful features offered by 
         REBEL.  They extend the power and capabilities of the 
         spreadsheet by allowing you to access functions, 
         utilities, and even full applications that can be tailored 
         to your specific needs.  They are also easy to use. 
         Simply, reference the library that contains the script(s)
         you want and REBEL's powerful Script Manager will handle 
         the rest for you.  For example, to access the scripts in 
         REBEL's standard library, STDLIB.REB, simply start the 
         program using the -L: option (followed immediately by the 
         name of the library): 
       
                           REBEL -L:STDLIB

         It's that simple!  The documentation for this library is 
         contained in STDLIB.DOC. 



    ___________________________________________________
    CHANGES (for existing users)

         The built-in FINANCIAL functions have been eliminated from
         this version of REBEL.  They're now scripts.  If you've
         used any of these functions in any of your worksheets, you
         will have to change their names to ALL UPPER CASE LETTERS.
         You will also have to 'attach' REBEL's standard script
         library file, STDLIB.REB, each time you start the program.
         To do this, use the -L: option (followed immediately by the
         name of the library):
       
                             REBEL -L:STDLIB



    ________________________________________________________
    WRITING YOUR OWN SCRIPTS

      All versions of REBEL 3.0 and higher come with a built-in Script 
      Manager that can access and execute scripts found in any (.REB)
      library file.  Writing and creating these libraries, however, is
      an optional feature that requires a license for REBEL's Script
      Library Builder.  The cost of this additional software is $29.00
      (see Order Form below). 


    ________________________________________________________
    KEEPING CURRENT

      There are two ways to make sure you have the latest version of
      REBEL:

      1)  If you have a licensed copy of the Script Library Builder
          (see Order Form below), you will automatically be notified
          when any new release becomes avaliable.

      2)  The latest release of REBEL is always posted on CompuServe
          in Library 6 (Business Apps) of the IBM Applications
          Forum (go IBMAPP) in a file called REBEL.ZIP.


 


